1. SWITCHES
performs three actions:learn,fload,forward
MAC ADDRESS TABLE : everything the switches know
switches consider everything after mac address or layer 2 as data 
switches uses ip address only when it needs to interact with a outside network like internet or router
switches interact with connected switches and devices through its respective ports 

Unicast Frame : destination MAC is another host
Switch will flood only if MAC address is not in MAC address table

Broadcast Frame : destination MAC address of FFFF.FFFF.FFFF
Broadcast frames are always Flooded
ex:ARP ----->  [ARP][L2]    where in L2 : Source mac address:_____   and Destination mac Address:FFFF:FFFF:FFFF

Switches will only send Broadcasts if traffic is going TO or FROM the Switch


